<span>Is microcurrent safe?</span>
              </button>
              <div id="FAQ-content-1649685536914b0d68-1" class="collapsible-content collapsible-content--all" style="height: 0px;">
                <div class="collapsible-content__inner collapsible-content__inner--faq rte">
                  <p>Microcurrent stimulates the muscles and activates them, while Invasive Treatments freezes the muscles. If you’ve just had Invasive Treatments done in a certain area, then you might need to avoid using microcurrent in that area, as it will start to undo the effect of Invasive Treatments. However, if you are in the phase where the effect of Invasive Treatments is running out, then microcurrent might be a better technology to use in that area to avoid usage of Invasive Treatments altogether. It will take some time but your muscles will reactivate and help build tone and firmness, instead of getting more laxed due to Invasive Treatments. There is no effect of microcurrent on Derma Fillers Treatment and it’s safe to use it. However, you should still consult your doctor.</p>
                </div>
              </div>
